  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b><size=+10>How To Play</size></b>

    1. Building in the Tableau

    Cards
    in the Tableau are stacked in descending order (from King to Ace) while alternating
    in colour.


    As seen below, you can place a Black 6 onto a Red 7, or a Black
    7 onto a Red 8. If you have a sequence of cards that already follow this rule
    (such as a Red 8, Black 7, and Red 6), you can move the entire group together
    onto a valid card (in this case, a Black 9). Whenever you move a card, if the
    remaining card is face-down, that card is flipped face-up.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7953b3aff3010de47827554b597de01f, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6622473957194473056, guid: 7953b3aff3010de47827554b597de01f, type: 2}
